    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The first government to unite the whole of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pohnpei">Pohnpei</a>, ruling from Nan Madol, a complex of nearly a hundred artificial islets of stacked basalt.</li><li>Its history is known from Pohnpeian oral tradition and archaeology; its dates and even the number of its rulers are uncertain.</li><li>Tradition says the hero <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isokelekel">Isokelekel</a> overthrew the last Saudeleur around 1628 and founded the Nahnmwarki chiefdoms that survive today.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Uranium-thorium dating of coral from the tomb of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pohnpei">Pohnpei</a>’s first island-wide ruler places its building at about 1180–1200, before monument building began on most other Pacific islands.</p></aside>
    </section>

